ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:1:# ZHEGLOV-SCOPE: Audit scoping for arXiv:2410.06959 v5 (DC(1))
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:3:Status: COMPLETE (2026-08-04). Scoping done; T1 falsification experiment since executed (see §6) — L:polynomials NOT REFUTED, 640/640.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:4:Artifacts: `zheglov/v5src/DC5.tex` (v5 source), `zheglov/abs_v1..v5.html` (version metadata).
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:7:Source: `zheglov/v5src/DC5.tex` (3539 lines). Sections + line ranges:
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:9:- **S2 Preliminaries, theory of normal forms** (565–1300, ~735 ln): imports from [A.Z]=Zheglov's generalized Schur theory, [GZ1]=Guo–Zheglov normal forms, Dixmier, Wilson, Sato. Ring tower A_1 ⊂ D_1=K[[x]][∂] ⊂ D̂_1^sym; Schur operator S with SPS⁻¹=∂^p; centralizer C(∂^p) ≅ M_p(K[D^p]), "vector form". Mostly cited, not reproved.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:13:- **S6 Proof of T:main** (2825–3539): 6a Preliminary lemmas (2842–3120): build modified pair P_n,Q_n then family Φ_{N,1}(P_n),Φ_{N,1}(Q_n) parametrized by N; **L:Phi_N(P)** (two cases, sequence lengths, distance head↔tail = N+1). 6b **"Some explicit calculations"** (3120–3539, ~420 ln): pass to Puiseux series X_{N,n} solving f(D̃^p,X)=0 (BC-type polynomial); **contradiction**: distinguished coefficient at D̃^{−ord P'} is N-independent (L:distinguished coefficients, via series-similarity X_{N1}=X_{N2}|_{D̃↦D̃^r}) yet Steps 4–7 compute it to be N-dependent. QED by contradiction.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:15:**Theorem chain:** ¬DC1 ⇒ subrectangular DC-pair [GGV, S3] ⇒ T:DC-pairs + T:subrectangular_sequence [S4] ⇒ family Φ_{N,1}-pairs with controlled sequences [L:Phi_N(P)] ⇒ string↔commutative correspondence [S5] transports to rank-1 spectral side ⇒ distinguished-coefficient computation contradicts N-independence [S6 Steps 4–7]. Normal forms (S2) are the ambient machinery for every step after S3.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:17:**External load-bearing inputs (not reproved here):** [GZ1] (arXiv 2303.10306, Guo–Zheglov normal forms — the whole calculus), [A.Z] (generalized Schur theory), [GGV] (subrectangular reduction of minimal counterexamples), Wilson's theorem, classical Schur–Sato. An error in [GZ1] would sink the paper wholesale.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:27:**R1. Endgame conjugation calculation, S6 Steps 4–7 (lines 3220–3390).** Hand symbolic computation in the bespoke vector-form calculus (Γ_1, Γ_2, σ-shifts, ∫-symbols): computes S̄_{−N−1}, γ_1=−a/(ln+Ndn)+dn/2, γ_2=−d_2/(2(Nd_2+l_2)), then E:tildeQ_N,I giving A=½d(M̃_{I−1}+1)(dn−M̃_{I−1}−1), B, C; then L:tail averaging; final c_{N,I;r(I)} formula. One sign/offset error anywhere destroys the contradiction. This is exactly the part "simplified" in v5 — i.e., rewritten twice (v4, v5). Includes the one-line inequality claim **A≠0** (line 3256, argument compressed: M̃_{I−1}=ord(Q_{I−1})nd−M_{I−1} forces dn−M̃_{I−1}−1≠0).
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:45:- New X items: @DavidTurturean asked S. Walters "do you regard this proof as correct?" already 2026-06-08 (pre-refutation); Walters (2026-07-22): can't judge, notes 78pp/4 updates/unrefereed. @ourtown2 (07-23) bare "Zheglov is correct" (~3 views, discount). Rest of Dixmier X traffic = DC(n≥3) fallout, not DC1 review.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:52:- **T0. Vector-form calculus kernel** (exact QQ, SymPy): homogeneous components, Γ_1/Γ_2, σ-shift, ∫-symbols, products, conjugation by elementary 1+s∫^i; validate against refereed [GZ1] identities (L:1, P:Si). ~6-10 agent-h. Prerequisite for T2/T3.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:53:- **T1. CHEAPEST FALSIFICATION EXPERIMENT: random-test L:polynomials** (line 1721). Unconditional polynomial claim: for g̃ with ≥2 distinct roots, c̃g̃^A = H'g̃−((z̃+1)/d̃)Hg̃' has a polynomial solution H only if l̃/d̃∈N, l̃/d̃>1, and then deg H=l̃(z̃+1)/d̃. Test = linear solve in coeffs of H over QQ for random (g̃,A,d̃,z̃=(A−1)d̃), including adversarial families (clustered roots, l̃/d̃ boundary cases). **~2-3 agent-h.** A single counterexample kills the S4 engine (used at lines 2041, 2198, 2301 to force the case exhaustions) ⇒ proof collapses.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:54:  - **EXECUTED 2026-08-04: NOT REFUTED.** 640/640 pass (exact ℚ; regimes l̃=d̃, l̃>d̃ with d̃∤l̃, l̃<d̃ nonexistence, d̃|l̃ with l̃/d̃≥2 degree claim; 9 genuinely solvable ≥2-root instances matched deg H = l̃(z̃+1)/d̃ exactly; 48/48 one-root controls). Untested: large parameters, off-rational moduli, lemma's internal induction. Log `ZHEGLOV-LTEST.md`, test `tests/ltest_polynomials.py`. Small positive update for the S4 engine; **T2 (Steps 4–7 symbolic replay) is now the live next action.**
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:55:- **T2. Symbolic replay of S6 Steps 4–7** (R1): recompute γ_1, γ_2, E:tildeQ_N,I, A/B/C, L:tail symmetrization, final c_{N,I;r(I)} with symbolic (N,d,l,n,m,M̃_{I−1},a,b); check A≠0 as an integer-constraint problem given S4's order bounds. ~15-25 agent-h. Highest expected-value check: freshest part (rewritten in v4 AND v5), pure computation, no vacuity problem.
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:60:**Totals: machine lane ~45-75 agent-hours; expert lane ~3-5 weeks. Verdict-relevant asymmetry: T1+T2 (~20-30 agent-h) could FALSIFY cheaply; corroboration of all risk steps cannot be finished by machine — R2/R3/R4 remain expert-gated.**
ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:61:**Decision note for campaign:** DC1 truth only closes the ¬DC1⇒¬JC2 refutation route; auditing Zheglov is *defensive* recon, not on our (72,108) critical path. Recommended spend: T1 now, T2 next; escalate to T3-T5 only if T1/T2 find anomalies or if we plan to cite DC1 as settled.
