xmodel/sol-census-review.md:215:For the conditional certificate, the answer is **yes, with that qualification**: any td-11 realization first reached above the degree-94 exact core is FC1; if it additionally requires `k>6` or lexicographic depth beyond 40, FC2 also applies. The naked abstract grammar row is not itself a td-11 configuration. FC1 therefore fail-closes the reachable threat; it does not rehabilitate the false global grammar lemma.
