xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:2956:ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:15:**Theorem chain:** ¬DC1 ⇒ subrectangular DC-pair [GGV, S3] ⇒ T:DC-pairs + T:subrectangular_sequence [S4] ⇒ family Φ_{N,1}-pairs with controlled sequences [L:Phi_N(P)] ⇒ string↔commutative correspondence [S5] transports to rank-1 spectral side ⇒ distinguished-coefficient computation contradicts N-independence [S6 Steps 4–7]. Normal forms (S2) are the ambient machinery for every step after S3.
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:2957:ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:17:**External load-bearing inputs (not reproved here):** [GZ1] (arXiv 2303.10306, Guo–Zheglov normal forms — the whole calculus), [A.Z] (generalized Schur theory), [GGV] (subrectangular reduction of minimal counterexamples), Wilson's theorem, classical Schur–Sato. An error in [GZ1] would sink the paper wholesale.
