# ZHEGLOV-SCOPE: Audit scoping for arXiv:2410.06959 v5 (DC(1))

Status: COMPLETE (2026-08-04). Scoping done; T1 falsification experiment since executed (see §6) — L:polynomials NOT REFUTED, 640/640.
Artifacts: `zheglov/v5src/DC5.tex` (v5 source), `zheglov/abs_v1..v5.html` (version metadata).

## 1. Paper architecture (v5)
Source: `zheglov/v5src/DC5.tex` (3539 lines). Sections + line ranges:
- **S1 Intro** (171–565): full proof scheme + notation list.
- **S2 Preliminaries, theory of normal forms** (565–1300, ~735 ln): imports from [A.Z]=Zheglov's generalized Schur theory, [GZ1]=Guo–Zheglov normal forms, Dixmier, Wilson, Sato. Ring tower A_1 ⊂ D_1=K[[x]][∂] ⊂ D̂_1^sym; Schur operator S with SPS⁻¹=∂^p; centralizer C(∂^p) ≅ M_p(K[D^p]), "vector form". Mostly cited, not reproved.
- **S3 DC-pairs** (1300–1451): counterexample = DC-pair; reduction to *subrectangular* Newton-polygon type (from [GGV] minimal-counterexample results); L:9 from [GZ] (Berest-conjecture paper).
- **S4 Main preparatory theorems** (1451–2357, ~906 ln, biggest): **T:DC-pairs** (head-chopping process terminates, distance maximal = p+q−1) and **T:subrectangular_sequence** (all F_i(P,Q) subrectangular; edge polynomials f_{0,1}, f_{1,0} identified). Inductive engine: L:Q_p (tail shape), **L:induction_step** (1575), **L:polynomials** (1721, "key lemma", uses subrectangularity), **L:induction_step1** (1853).
- **S5 String equation** (2357–2825, added in v4): [Q,P]=1 for general ODOs; bijection {string solutions with terminating head-chopping} ↔ {rank-1 commuting pairs} via cutting/glueing the tail (T:string_equation 2547, T:one-to-one-correspondence 2620/2727, T:inverse_string_equation 2748). Extends A. Schwarz's coprime-order correspondence to **non-coprime orders** — needed because subrectangular DC-pairs have non-coprime orders.
- **S6 Proof of T:main** (2825–3539): 6a Preliminary lemmas (2842–3120): build modified pair P_n,Q_n then family Φ_{N,1}(P_n),Φ_{N,1}(Q_n) parametrized by N; **L:Phi_N(P)** (two cases, sequence lengths, distance head↔tail = N+1). 6b **"Some explicit calculations"** (3120–3539, ~420 ln): pass to Puiseux series X_{N,n} solving f(D̃^p,X)=0 (BC-type polynomial); **contradiction**: distinguished coefficient at D̃^{−ord P'} is N-independent (L:distinguished coefficients, via series-similarity X_{N1}=X_{N2}|_{D̃↦D̃^r}) yet Steps 4–7 compute it to be N-dependent. QED by contradiction.

**Theorem chain:** ¬DC1 ⇒ subrectangular DC-pair [GGV, S3] ⇒ T:DC-pairs + T:subrectangular_sequence [S4] ⇒ family Φ_{N,1}-pairs with controlled sequences [L:Phi_N(P)] ⇒ string↔commutative correspondence [S5] transports to rank-1 spectral side ⇒ distinguished-coefficient computation contradicts N-independence [S6 Steps 4–7]. Normal forms (S2) are the ambient machinery for every step after S3.

**External load-bearing inputs (not reproved here):** [GZ1] (arXiv 2303.10306, Guo–Zheglov normal forms — the whole calculus), [A.Z] (generalized Schur theory), [GGV] (subrectangular reduction of minimal counterexamples), Wilson's theorem, classical Schur–Sato. An error in [GZ1] would sink the paper wholesale.

## 2. Version history v1→v5
- v1 2024-10-09, 25 pp. v2 2024-10-14 "minor changes".
- v3 2024-10-23, 34 pp: "improved exposition, more details to the proof added".
- v4 2025-02-17, 67 pp: "significantly improved version: investigation of solutions to the string equation is added" — paper doubles; S5 correspondence machinery added, presumably to repair/rigorize the transport step from Weyl pairs to spectral series.
- v5 2026-01-19, 78 pp: "extended introduction, more comments and references added, **calculations at the last stage of the proof are simplified**, some typos fixed".
- Read: 25→78 pp with the contradiction-stage calculation reworked twice (v4, v5). v5 thanks "anonymous referees" (who pointed out Schwarz's papers) ⇒ under journal review; referee round(s) happened but no acceptance signal. Author also thanks Makar-Limanov, Valqui (of GGV), Junhu Guo.

## 3. Top risk steps (3-5)
**R1. Endgame conjugation calculation, S6 Steps 4–7 (lines 3220–3390).** Hand symbolic computation in the bespoke vector-form calculus (Γ_1, Γ_2, σ-shifts, ∫-symbols): computes S̄_{−N−1}, γ_1=−a/(ln+Ndn)+dn/2, γ_2=−d_2/(2(Nd_2+l_2)), then E:tildeQ_N,I giving A=½d(M̃_{I−1}+1)(dn−M̃_{I−1}−1), B, C; then L:tail averaging; final c_{N,I;r(I)} formula. One sign/offset error anywhere destroys the contradiction. This is exactly the part "simplified" in v5 — i.e., rewritten twice (v4, v5). Includes the one-line inequality claim **A≠0** (line 3256, argument compressed: M̃_{I−1}=ord(Q_{I−1})nd−M_{I−1} forces dn−M̃_{I−1}−1≠0).
**R2. N-independence lemma (L:distinguished coefficients, 3168–3210).** The other jaw of the contradiction. Subtle order-bookkeeping on which monomials of X_{N,k−1}^p can contribute at order r(k); separate delicate special case M_{I−1}=d_2=2 (l_2=1) using vanishing (Q_{N,I})_{ord−1}=0. If a monomial slips the inequality E:inequality_for_j, N-independence fails and there is no contradiction.
**R3. S4 preparatory induction (T:DC-pairs + T:subrectangular_sequence, 1517–2357, ~840 lines).** Long induction with repetitive case exhaustions ("this case is impossible" at 2241, 2350); each step invokes L:polynomials with specific parameter substitutions (A, d̃, l̃, z̃) plus divisibility forcing d/l=d_2. Author himself flags: proofs "often similar or even repetitive... described in detail to avoid errors". Distance=p+q−1 exactly (E:distance) is the quantitative output later needed in S6.
**R4. String-equation correspondence for NON-coprime orders (S5, esp. T:one-to-one-correspondence & inverse, 2620–2790).** Extends A. Schwarz's coprime-order bijection; needed precisely because subrectangular DC-pairs have non-coprime orders. Feeds R:distinguished_coefficient (distinguished coefficient =0, via Newton–Puiseux + Wilson, rank-1). Formal-series existence/uniqueness/normalization arguments; the whole transport of the DC-pair to the Puiseux-series side rests here.
**R5. L:Phi_N(P) (2919–3120, ~200 lines).** Two-case analysis of how the Φ_{N,1}-family's head-chopping sequence relates to the original (lengths, ε_i equality, ord Q_{N,i}=(d_2N+l_2)ord(Q_i)/d_2, distance head↔tail = N+1). Both R1 and R2 consume its formulas; "relies heavily" on R3.
Lower risk: S2 imports ([GZ1] "to appear in Izvestiya" = refereed; [A.Z] published Steklov Proc.; [GGV] published J.Algebra 2014 — Prop 6.9 subrectangular reduction, Th 4.1(3)).

## 4. Checkability per risk step
- **R1 → (a) computation.** Fully mechanizable: implement the graded D̂_1^sym / vector-form calculus (finite data per homogeneous component: p×p vector + Γ-polynomial coefficients) in SymPy/exact QQ. Verify E:tildeQ_N,I and A,B,C symbolically in (N,d,l,n,M̃,a,b); verify γ_1,γ_2; verify L:tail symmetrization sum; verify A≠0 under the stated integer constraints. Independent consistency check available: Γ_1-coefficient −(d−l)/(dN+l) in E:tildeQ_N,I must equal tail's (dn−ln)/p̃ with p̃=n(dN+l) — it does (good sign, and shows such invariants are testable).
- **R2 → (a)+(c).** The inequality bookkeeping is finite arithmetic per (k); scriptable for symbolic parameters; the special case is checkable. But "expressions coincide because F_i coincide" needs expert reading of R:relation_between_coeff provenance.
- **R3 → (a) spot-check + (c).** L:polynomials itself: pure polynomial-ODE claim — test by random g̃, A, d̃, z̃ over QQ (linear algebra in coefficients of H). Induction superstructure: expert reading; formalization-scale if attempted fully (b).
- **R4 → (c), partial (a).** Correspondence theorems are conceptual; but cutting/glueing the tail is algorithmic on truncated series — can numerically instantiate: take explicit commuting rank-1 pairs (e.g. KdV/Burchnall–Chaundy pairs), glue tail, check [Q,P]=1 to finite order, and vice versa. Distinguished-coefficient=0 claim testable on explicit rank-1 examples.
- **R5 → (a) spot-check + (c).** Order/GCD formulas testable on synthetic subrectangular pairs *if* candidate DC-pair surrogates exist (none do — vacuous domain; test instead on the automorphism examples where the machinery applies with non-maximal distance, cf. R:spectral_data_for_string).
- **Global obstacle for (a):** all S4/S6 statements quantify over hypothetical DC-pairs (empty set if theorem true). Directly instantiable objects: automorphism pairs (φ(x),φ(∂)), string-equation solutions in D_1, commuting rank-1 pairs. Falsification target must be a lemma whose hypotheses these NON-vacuous objects satisfy: L:polynomials (any polynomials), S5 correspondence (any string solution), L:Q_p tail shape (any normalized P plus Q with [Q,P]=1 — automorphism pairs qualify!).

## 5. Public discussion beyond RECON.md
Delta findings (2026-08-04 sweep: WebSearch + grok/X):
- **Zero substantive technical engagement found anywhere.** No named Weyl-algebra specialist publicly walking the proof; no reported gap; no formalization attempt; no journal acceptance news.
- New X items: @DavidTurturean asked S. Walters "do you regard this proof as correct?" already 2026-06-08 (pre-refutation); Walters (2026-07-22): can't judge, notes 78pp/4 updates/unrefereed. @ourtown2 (07-23) bare "Zheglov is correct" (~3 views, discount). Rest of Dixmier X traffic = DC(n≥3) fallout, not DC1 review.
- **Positive de-risking discovered:** the machinery papers are refereed — [GZ1] I (2406.14414, v4 Nov 2025) AND II (2511.05117) both "to appear in Izvestiya: Mathematics"; "Normal forms III" published in Proc. Steklov. [A.Z] published Steklov 2023; [GGV] J.Algebra 2014. So only DC5's own reasoning is unrefereed. v5 thanks **anonymous referees** ⇒ at least one journal round happened by Jan 2026; no acceptance 6+ months later.
- Flag: [GZ1] split into I/II at v4 (Nov 2025), after DC5 v4 — verify each of the ~15 cited [GZ1] lemma numbers (Lem 2.5–3.4, Th 2.2, Cor 2.1–2.3) still lands in refereed part I, not part II.
- MathOverflow + Reddit remain crawler-blocked [GAP, same as RECON]; manual browser check still recommended.

## 6. Audit plan
Ordered verification tasks (machine lane first; each falsifies-or-corroborates):
- **T0. Vector-form calculus kernel** (exact QQ, SymPy): homogeneous components, Γ_1/Γ_2, σ-shift, ∫-symbols, products, conjugation by elementary 1+s∫^i; validate against refereed [GZ1] identities (L:1, P:Si). ~6-10 agent-h. Prerequisite for T2/T3.
- **T1. CHEAPEST FALSIFICATION EXPERIMENT: random-test L:polynomials** (line 1721). Unconditional polynomial claim: for g̃ with ≥2 distinct roots, c̃g̃^A = H'g̃−((z̃+1)/d̃)Hg̃' has a polynomial solution H only if l̃/d̃∈N, l̃/d̃>1, and then deg H=l̃(z̃+1)/d̃. Test = linear solve in coeffs of H over QQ for random (g̃,A,d̃,z̃=(A−1)d̃), including adversarial families (clustered roots, l̃/d̃ boundary cases). **~2-3 agent-h.** A single counterexample kills the S4 engine (used at lines 2041, 2198, 2301 to force the case exhaustions) ⇒ proof collapses.
  - **EXECUTED 2026-08-04: NOT REFUTED.** 640/640 pass (exact ℚ; regimes l̃=d̃, l̃>d̃ with d̃∤l̃, l̃<d̃ nonexistence, d̃|l̃ with l̃/d̃≥2 degree claim; 9 genuinely solvable ≥2-root instances matched deg H = l̃(z̃+1)/d̃ exactly; 48/48 one-root controls). Untested: large parameters, off-rational moduli, lemma's internal induction. Log `ZHEGLOV-LTEST.md`, test `tests/ltest_polynomials.py`. Small positive update for the S4 engine; **T2 (Steps 4–7 symbolic replay) is now the live next action.**
- **T2. Symbolic replay of S6 Steps 4–7** (R1): recompute γ_1, γ_2, E:tildeQ_N,I, A/B/C, L:tail symmetrization, final c_{N,I;r(I)} with symbolic (N,d,l,n,m,M̃_{I−1},a,b); check A≠0 as an integer-constraint problem given S4's order bounds. ~15-25 agent-h. Highest expected-value check: freshest part (rewritten in v4 AND v5), pure computation, no vacuity problem.
- **T3. Machinery on non-vacuous objects**: automorphism pairs (φ(x),φ(∂)) in A_1 and Burchnall–Chaundy rank-1 commuting pairs; compute normal forms to finite order; test L:Q_p tail shape, termination + non-maximal distance (intro's claim), S5 cut/glue roundtrip, distinguished-coefficient=0 (R:distinguished_coefficient). ~10-20 agent-h. Tests R4 + S2 end-to-end where hypotheses are satisfiable.
- **T4. Arithmetic of L:distinguished coefficients** (R2): encode order-inequality bookkeeping (E:inequality_for_j, special case M_{I−1}=d_2=2) for symbolic parameters via SMT/Presburger-style checks. ~10-15 agent-h; residual "expressions coincide" provenance needs expert.
- **T5. Expert reading**: S4 induction (R3, ~840 lines, 1-2 wk), S5 correspondence (R4, ~1 wk), L:Phi_N(P) + interface to [GGV] Prop 6.9 minimality (0.5 wk). Total **~3-5 expert-weeks**. Natural experts: Valqui/Makar-Limanov (already in contact with author — nonindependent), Bavula, Han–Tan group, A. Schwarz (S5).
- **T6 (optional). Formalization**: not recommended — needs [GZ1] I+II first; est. 6-12 expert-months.
