   510	4. The Newton Polygon of a polynomial $f(x,y)=\sum c_{ij}x^{i}y^{j}\in K[x,y]$ is the convex hull of all the points $(i,j)$ with respect to those $c_{ij}\neq 0$.
   511	
   512	Following \cite{Dixmier}, we define $E(f)=\{(i,j)|c_{ij}\neq 0 \}$ as the point set of the Newton Polygon. Suppose $\sigma, \rho$ are two real numbers, we define the weight degree $v_{\sigma,\rho}(f)$: 
   513	$$v_{\sigma,\rho}(f)=sup\{\sigma i+\rho j|(i,j)\in E(f)\}, \quad E(f,\sigma,\rho)=\{(i,j)|v_{\sigma,\rho}(f)=\sigma i +\rho j \}.$$
   514	
