   790	Let $P\in D_1$ be a normalized operator of positive degree, i.e. $P=\partial^k + c_{k-2}\partial^{k-2}+\ldots + c_0$, $k>0$. Then there exists an operator $S$ from item 1 such that $S_0=1$, $S_{-1}=0$. 
   791		\end{enumerate}
   792		
   793	We'll call the operator $S$ from item 1 as a Schur operator for $P\in  \hat{D}^{sym}_{1}$, and the operator $S$ from item 2 as a Schur operator for {\it normalized differential operator} $P\in D_1$. 	
   794	\end{Prop}
