   896	Denote by
   897	$$
   898	Hcpc(k):=\{\text{all HCPCs assoicated to }k\}
   899	$$
   900	the subring from corollary. 
   901	It's easy to observe that if $a|b$, $b=ra$ and $\xi,\eta$ are respectively  the $a,b$-primitive roots, then $\eta^r=\xi$, i.e. $A_{b,ir}=A_{a,i}$. This means
   902	$$
   903	Hcpc(a)\subseteq Hcpc(b)
   904	$$
   905	Thus for $p,q$, if we assume $r=gcd(p,q)$, then we have 
   906	$$
   907	Hcpc(p)\bigcap Hcpc(q)\supseteq Hcpc(r).
   908	$$
