  1142	Note also that the modules $W$ and $F$ are isomorphic ($W$ is an $A$-module, $F$ as a $B$-module, and clearly $A\simeq B$). For convenience of notation, we will replace $\partial^{-1}$ by $z$ in the field $K((\partial^{-1}))$, i.e. $A,W\subset K((z))\simeq K((\partial^{-1}))$. 
  1143	
