    <h1 class="title mathjax"><span class="descriptor">Title:</span>The Conjecture of Dixmier for the first Weyl algebra is true</h1>
    <div class="authors"><span class="descriptor">Authors:</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/math?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zheglov,+A" rel="nofollow">Alexander Zheglov</a></div>            <div id="download-button-info" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled The Conjecture of Dixmier for the first Weyl algebra is true, by Alexander Zheglov</div>
    <a class="mobile-submission-download" href="/pdf/2410.06959v5">View PDF</a>



    <blockquote class="abstract mathjax">
            <span class="descriptor">Abstract:</span>Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $A_1=K[x][\partial ]$ be the first Weyl algebra. In this paper we prove that the Dixmier conjecture for the first Weyl algebra is true, i.e. each algebra endomorphism of the algebra $A_1$ is an automorphism.
    </blockquote>

