3148:{\it Step} 3.  For simplicity of further calculations let's take a sequence of polynomials $F_i(X,Y)$ for initial operators $P,Q$ from section \ref{S:prelim_lemmas} for which $n_i=p$ for all $i$ (see theorem \ref{T:DC-pairs} for notation). To fix notation, let $(\ord Q_i, \epsilon_i )$, $i=0, \ldots ,I$ be the corresponding sequence for the pair $P,Q$. Then by lemma \ref{L:Phi_N(P)} there exists similar sequence $(\ord Q_{N,i}, \epsilon_i )$ also for the pair $\Phi_{N,1}(P_n), \Phi_{N,1}(Q_n)$ (with the same $\epsilon_i$ for $i=0, \ldots ,I$). Below we'll continue to use notations from lemma \ref{L:Phi_N(P)} and assume $N>1$. 
